## 2. Core Gameplay

### 2.1 Match Structure
- Best of three rounds, 60-second timer.
- Vitality is 1000 points. A typical round lasts 35–50 seconds.
- A round has no loading and restarts instantly. Round transitions are beat-synced wipes so the trance never breaks.
- **Final Round Eclipse.** In round three, each stage shifts into its most extreme color script.

### 2.2 Controls
Six buttons. Two input schemes ship in the box:
- **Duelist (Classic):** motion inputs (quarter-circles and similar). Arcade-stick friendly.
- **Ritual (Simplified):** one-button specials and an auto-combo. It plays on the same rules, just with an easier route to the same moves, and it is fully legal in online play.

| Button | Function |
|---|---|
| Light Slash | Fast, low-damage, links and cancels |
| Heavy Slash | Slow, high-damage, costs 6 Resolve |
| Kick | Body strikes: low sweeps, launchers, pushbacks |
| Curse Art | Character-defining moves, performed with a hand-seal pose; inflicts Fester |
| Guard | Block (hold) / Severance (tap) |
| Trance | Spend gauge: Curse Cancel, Rite, Possession |

Extra inputs:
- **Seize (throw):** Light + Kick.
- **Roll:** Guard + Kick. 20 frames, invulnerable on frames 4–16, costs 20 Resolve (20% of the bar).

### 2.3 Attack Tells (Readability Code)
Each weapon has a flicker of colored light at the instant of commitment. Each color also has a distinct shape for colorblind players.
- **White glint (circle):** standard mid.
- **Gold glint (diamond):** overhead (stand-block only).
- **Blue glint (wedge):** low (crouch-block only).
- **Red glint (jagged):** *Maledict* (guard-unblockable). It must be rolled, jumped, or beaten with a Severance. This is the only unblockable class, and it always telegraphs for at least 20 frames.

### 2.4 Resources
**Vitality** (1000)
- Light hits do 28–40, heavies 80–120, Rites 280–380.
- Combos typically land 220–380 after scaling, and a "decisive cut" counter-hit can cost 30–40% of the bar (300–400).

**Resolve** (100)
- It drains when blocking: a light costs 8 and a heavy costs 18. Rolling costs 20 and a Heavy Slash costs 6.
- It regenerates at about 12 per second when idle (not while blocking).
- At zero the fighter is **Staggered** for 90 frames (1.5 s, dizzy, open to a free punish), then returns at 40 Resolve.
- The HUD shows it as a thin silver thread that frays and sparks as it depletes.

**Trance Gauge** (3 stocks, shown as a bead strand)
- It fills from attacking, landing Sync Hits, and Severance. It does not fill during Possession.
- Spend 1 for an EX Curse Art or a **Curse Cancel** (cancel any move on hit, block, or whiff into neutral).
- Spend 2 for a **Rite** (cinematic super).
- Spend 3 for **Possession**.

### 2.5 Fester (the Curse Bargain)
- Curse Arts and Rites inflict **Fester**. Part of the damage is deferred and appears as a violet, glyph-crawling segment on the victim's Vitality bar.
- After **5 seconds** (300 frames), any remaining Fester becomes real damage.
- The victim cleans it by **landing any hit** (clears a chunk) or by **Severance** (clears the remainder).
- The attacker can detonate Fester early with **Reap**: any Heavy Slash on a Festering target converts a portion instantly, with a signature "seal-burst" FX.
- The attacker is rewarded for pressure and the defender for counter-aggression. Turtling is a losing strategy.

### 2.6 The Tempo (the Shared Arc)
A match-wide meter from 0 to 100, shown as a glowing halo ring around the timer. It has three phases.

| Phase | Range | Effects |
|---|---|---|
| **Prelude** | 0–33 | Baseline. Sparse half-time music. |
| **Rupture** | 34–66 | +5% damage, Pulse windows widen, breakbeat music. |
| **Frenzy** | 67–100 | +10% damage, +20% Resolve damage, +25% Trance gain, double-time music, stage overload. |

- Tempo rises with hits, blocks, Severances and Sync Hits.
- It also has timer floors: at **40 s remaining** it is raised to at least 34 (Rupture), and at **20 s remaining** to at least 67 (Frenzy).
- It **ratchets**: it may fluctuate inside a phase but never drops to a lower phase within the round.
- Every round resolves as a rising arc.

### 2.7 The Pulse (the Heartbeat)
- A giant stage sigil pulses on the beat, visible on the floor and at the HUD ring edges.
- A hit landing within ±3 frames of the Pulse (a 7-frame window) is a **Sync Hit**, worth +2 hitstop frames, +50% Trance gain, a bell-chime in the stage's key, and a lotus-petal-burst FX.
- It is never required, and an option can disable it.
- Training Mode includes a metronome.

### 2.8 Severance (Just Guard)
- Tapping Guard in the 8-frame window before a hit is a **Severance**. It also works against Maledict attacks.
- The attacker's weapon is deflected, with a ring of sparks.
- **Hush:** the music low-passes into a resonant drone and the screen desaturates for about 0.5 seconds. On your first counter-input the music slams back at full volume with a bass drop.
- A miss costs 15 Resolve and 20 frames of recovery.
- A Severance clears all Fester.

### 2.9 Blade Lock (Clash)
When both fighters swing into each other in the same frame window, the weapons lock.
- Each player picks **Push** (Heavy), **Slip** (Roll) or **Pull** (Kick), as rock-paper-scissors: Push beats Pull, Pull beats Slip, Slip beats Push.
- The pick must be made within 20 frames.
- A tie is resolved by whoever is closer to the Pulse.

### 2.10 Possession (the Awakened State)
- Costs 3 Trance stocks and lasts about 12 seconds.
- Each character transforms visually, usually with a halo, an aureole or a spectral beast, and gains unique rules (see roster).
- When it ends, **Backlash** converts 10% of the user's max Vitality (100 points) into self-inflicted Fester.
- If the opponent clears the Fester, the Backlash is wasted. Possession is a gamble.

### 2.11 Feel Targets
- **Hitstop:** light 6f, heavy 11f, counter-hit +4f, Sync Hit +2f, Rite finisher 24f plus two impact frames.
- **Input buffer:** 5f.
- **Camera:** it nudges toward the point of impact on heavy hits.
- **Smear frames** on all swings, with ribbon-scarf trails on cloth.
- **Impact frames:** a two-frame inverted ink flash on heavy hits, decisive cuts, and Rite finishers. It is subtle on ordinary hits.
- Controller rumble is tied to the Pulse during Frenzy, so the pad "breathes" with the music.

