## 11. Quality Bar (Design-Level Gates)

Every character, move, stage and UI element must pass:
- **Silhouette test:** every move reads as a unique shape, including halos, ribbons and spectral arms.
- **Mute test:** every hit and tell can be read with the sound off.
- **Squint test:** the screen's value structure reads at a glance.
- **Three-second test:** a new viewer can tell who is winning within three seconds.
- **Roster test:** every fighter reads as an adult (20+) in every outfit, and no fighter reads as male. Armored fighters must not signal gender through silhouette, voice or text.
- **Guardrail test:** no real-world faith figures, named deities, scripture, clergy or ritual acts appear in names, art, text or audio. All motifs are abstracted into invented iconography (§0.1).
- **Fairness rules:** no unblockable without a tell, no infinites, and every Maledict has at least 20 frames of warning.
- **Feel review:** every move is reviewed for anticipation, impact and follow-through before sign-off.
- **Polish pass:** consistent line weights, palette discipline, and a final audio mix against all three Tempo phases.
